          "title": "Compositional Generalization via Structural Identification in a Category-Theoretic Framework",
          "title_zh": "范畴论框架下通过结构辨识实现组合泛化",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.26465v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2608.26465",
          "summary": "Represents sentences as functors from syntactic addresses to lexical tokens and uses selective collapses that induce Kan extensions to ask which structural or lexical identifications make held-out COGS examples admissible given the structures observed in training. Across 21 COGS generalization types, admissibility follows distinct identification profiles while residual failures separate unsupported structural templates, all without training a predictive model.",
