          "title": "Subgraph Filtering for Fair Graph Neural Networks",
          "title_zh": "面向公平图神经网络的子图过滤",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.26437v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2608.26437",
          "summary": "Proposes SF-GNN, a lightweight architecture-agnostic framework that identifies bias-prone edges by combining sensitive homophily with structural propagation amplifiers such as hub participation and triadic closure, then applies stochastic edge filtering at each message-passing step while adding a statistical-parity regularizer with a warm-up schedule. Experiments on five benchmark datasets show consistent fairness improvements with competitive predictive performance, yielding a better fairness-accuracy trade-off than recent fairness-aware GNN baselines.",
