        {
          "title": "Don't Overthink, Don't Underthink: Toward Adaptive Reasoning in Agentic AI",
          "title_zh": "别过度思考，也别思考不足：迈向智能体 AI 的自适应推理",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.26442v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2608.26442",
          "summary": "Argues that fixed or pre-allocated reasoning controls are poorly suited to agentic systems, where reasoning demands evolve through planning, tool use, memory retrieval, and agent-to-agent interaction, and characterizes over-reasoning and under-reasoning as recurring failure modes of misallocated reasoning. Evaluating on MATH-500 and the GAIA public validation benchmark, the authors find over-reasoning cases incur higher computational cost without proportional accuracy gains, while under-reasoning cases are consistently associated with incorrect or incomplete solutions.",
