          "title": "Vowel Signs Are Not Letters: A Pre-tokenization Ceiling on Multilingual Tokenizer Fertility",
          "title_zh": "元音符号不是字母：多语言分词器“生育率”的预分词上限",
          "url": "http://arxiv.org/abs/2608.26449v1",
          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2608.26449",
          "summary": "Formalizes a training-free lower bound on tokenizer fertility caused by the GPT-2-derived letters-only word regex, which splits abugida words at every combining vowel sign so that BPE merges can never rejoin them regardless of vocabulary size or corpus mix. Across 26 languages all 17 abugidas are affected (1.47× for Tibetan to 9.02× for Thai), three matched 268M models show the fixed tokenizer gaining 4.43% in held-out Nepali bits per byte, and a census finds the pattern in 63.3% of the most-downloaded text-generation models.",
