          "source": "arXiv",
          "section": "arxiv_other",
          "organization": "",
          "language": "en",
          "arxiv_id": "2608.26451",
          "summary": "Proposes FairGIN, a fairness-aware graph neural network for bike-sharing demand prediction that combines expansion-simulated increment training to narrow the cold-start gap, attention-based knowledge transfer from data-rich to new stations, and income-stratified regularization with an equity-calibrated deployment score. Experiments on NYC and Seattle report state-of-the-art accuracy across expansion scenarios while substantially reducing income-based disparities without compromising overall system efficiency.",
